Translation refusal (e.g., safety filters, content policy violations) previously terminated file processing, losing all subsequent items. Now returns original text and continues processing.

## Changes

**Error handling in `processLanguageFile`** (scripts/factory/translate.ts)
- `TranslationRefusedError` now returns source text with null hash instead of throwing `TranslationRefusalStopError`
- Processing continues to next items in same file and across all files
- Refused items tracked in `untranslatedItems` for GitHub issue generation

**Removed `TranslationRefusalStopError` class**
- No longer needed; simplified Promise.allSettled result handling

**Test updates**
- 3 test cases verify refused items preserve original text and don't block subsequent processing

## Example

```typescript
// Before: Translation refused at key_5, key_6-key_9 lost
try {
  translatedValue = await translate(sourceValue, gameType, 0, undefined, shouldTransliterate)
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof TranslationRefusedError) {
    throw new TranslationRefusalStopError(...)  // Stops processing
  }
}

// After: Translation refused at key_5, key_6-key_9 processed normally
try {
  translatedValue = await translate(sourceValue, gameType, 0, undefined, shouldTransliterate)
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof TranslationRefusedError) {
    translatedValue = sourceValue  // Keep original
    hashForEntry = null            // Allow retry
    untranslatedItems.push(...)    // Track for issues
    // Continue to next item
  }
}
```

All 395 tests pass.

