X.com's DOM structure changed in late 2025, causing zero detection due to invisible characters being split across text nodes when scanning the entire page.

## Changes

**Detection Strategy**
- Scope to `article[data-testid="tweet"]` containers on X.com/Twitter
- Aggregate all text nodes within `[data-testid="tweetText"]` during detection phase
- Validate complete messages (both `\uFEFF` delimiters present) before returning results
- Fall back to page-wide scanning for non-X.com sites

**Twitter Adapter**
- Simplified from 80+ lines to 15 lines
- Removed 15-level parent traversal and programmatic extraction fallbacks
- Detection now provides complete aggregated text, adapter just re-validates from tweetText container

**Timing**
- `INITIAL_SCAN_DELAY`: 2s → 3s
- `SECONDARY_SCAN_DELAY`: 5s → 8s

## Implementation

```javascript
// New tweet-scoped detection for X.com
const isXCom = hostname === 'x.com' || hostname === 'twitter.com';

if (isXCom) {
    const tweetArticles = document.querySelectorAll('article[data-testid="tweet"]');
    tweetArticles.forEach(article => {
